{"seq":9,"slug":"threads-concurrency","title":"线程与并发","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":8,"docCount":26,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency","rating":{"composite":4.33,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.6,"coverage":4.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.52,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"线程与并发-简介\">线程与并发 简介</h1><p>现代软件系统几乎无一例外地需要同时处理多项任务。无论是操作系统在后台调度数十个服务，还是移动应用一边渲染界面一边请求网络数据，并发编程都是支撑这一切的基石。理解并发不仅仅是掌握几个 API，更需要从底层原理出发，建立对执行模型、资源竞争和同步协调的系统性认知。</p>\n<p>本手册以&quot;线程与并发&quot;为主题，从最基础的操作系统概念一路延伸到高级并发模型，力求帮助读者构建完整的并发知识体系。</p>\n<p>手册面向已具备基本编程经验、希望深入理解并发机制的开发者。你不需要是操作系统专家，但应当对程序的编译、运行有初步了解。无论你日常使用何种编程语言，本手册讨论的原理和思想都具有普适价值。</p>\n<p>全书共分为八个章节，建议按顺序阅读：</p>\n<p>第一章&quot;进程&quot;从操作系统的资源分配单位讲起，帮助你理解程序如何被加载、执行和管理。进程是并发世界的起点，掌握它的概念才能理解后续更轻量的执行单元。</p>\n<p>第二章&quot;线程&quot;引入操作系统调度的基本单位。线程共享进程的地址空间，带来了更高效的并发能力，同时也引入了数据竞争等复杂问题。</p>\n<p>第三章&quot;协程&quot;介绍用户态的轻量级并发原语。协程由程序自身控制调度，开销极低，是现代异步编程的核心手段。</p>\n<p>第四章&quot;并发与并行&quot;厘清两个经常被混淆的概念，并讨论它们在不同硬件架构下的实现方式和设计策略。</p>\n<p>第五章&quot;原子操作&quot;深入到硬件层面，探讨无锁编程的基础。理解原子操作和内存序是编写高性能并发代码的关键。</p>\n<p>第六章&quot;锁&quot;系统地介绍互斥锁、读写锁、自旋锁等同步原语，分析它们的适用场景与性能取舍。</p>\n<p>第七章&quot;Actor 模型&quot;展示一种消息驱动的并发架构。Actor 模型通过消除共享状态从根本上规避了许多传统并发难题。</p>\n<p>第八章&quot;补充主题&quot;汇集竞态条件、死锁、信号量、线程池、消息传递等实践中不可回避的重要话题，作为前七章的有力补充。</p>\n<p>建议从第一章顺序推进，前三章建立执行单元的认知基础，第四章形成宏观视角，第五至七章掌握具体的同步与并发工具，最后通过第八章将知识串联为实战能力。</p>\n<p>祝你在并发编程的世界中走得更远、更稳。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"processes","title":"进程","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/processes","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"process-definition-and-concepts","title":"进程的定义与核心概念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/processes/process-definition-and-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"process-core-ideas","title":"进程的核心思想","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/processes/process-core-ideas"},{"seq":3,"slug":"process-implementation","title":"进程的实现机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/processes/process-implementation"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"threads","title":"线程","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/threads","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"thread-definition-and-concepts","title":"线程的定义与核心概念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/threads/thread-definition-and-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"thread-core-ideas","title":"线程的核心思想","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/threads/thread-core-ideas"},{"seq":3,"slug":"thread-implementation","title":"线程的实现机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/threads/thread-implementation"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"coroutines","title":"协程","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/coroutines","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"coroutine-definition-and-concepts","title":"协程的定义与核心概念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/coroutines/coroutine-definition-and-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"coroutine-core-ideas","title":"协程的核心思想","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/coroutines/coroutine-core-ideas"},{"seq":3,"slug":"coroutine-implementation","title":"协程的实现机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/coroutines/coroutine-implementation"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"concurrency-and-parallelism","title":"并发与并行","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/concurrency-and-parallelism","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"concurrency-parallelism-concepts","title":"并发与并行的核心概念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/concurrency-and-parallelism/concurrency-parallelism-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"concurrency-parallelism-ideas","title":"并发与并行的核心思想","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/threads-concurrency/concurrency-and-parallelism/concurrency-parallelism-ideas"},{"seq":3,"slug":"concurrency-parallelism-implementation","title":"并发与并行的实现机制","url":"/l-do